<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Cycle</strong> Monthly, billed on the anniversary of the agreement signing date</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Primary owner; no separate accounting team</div>
  <div><strong>Tools</strong> Stripe (card-on-file recurring) + manual ACH for clients who prefer</div>
  <div><strong>Late SLA</strong> Day-3 reminder, day-7 follow-up, day-15 hold notice, day-30 service pause</div>
</div>

<h2>The monthly cycle</h2>

<h3>Day -7 (week before billing day)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Glance at the active-clients spreadsheet. Confirm billing days, plan tiers, card-on-file status.</li>
  <li>Note any scheduled plan changes that should hit this cycle.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day 0 (billing day)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Stripe auto-charges card-on-file clients overnight.</li>
  <li>For ACH clients: send invoice via email at 9am MT with a 7-day net.</li>
  <li>Verify all charges succeeded. Note any declines.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day +1</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>If a card-on-file client's charge declined: email them within 24 hours, polite tone. "Your card got declined; happy to take a different one or send an invoice for ACH."</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day +3</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Reminder for ACH clients who haven't paid yet. Polite, no charge.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day +7</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Second follow-up. Slightly firmer. Mention the agreement-stipulated late fee if applicable.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day +15</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Hold notice. "Service will be paused on day 30 if not resolved." Phone call if they don't reply to email.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Day +30</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>If still unpaid: pause service per agreement. Site stays up (we don't punish their visitors); content updates and emergency support are on hold until paid.</li>
  <li>Document in CRM. Don't take it personally.</li>
</ul>

